# Block Drop — Terraform

## Layout

- AWS site module: `infra/terraform/aws/modules/site`
- Env roots: `infra/terraform/aws/envs/stg`, `envs/prod`
- Shared state bootstrap: `infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap`
- Cloudflare DNS: `infra/terraform/cloudflare` (own root, same S3 backend)
- Grafana Cloud observability: `infra/terraform/grafana` (own root, same S3 backend)

## Naming

AWS names: `[environment]-block-drop-[purpose]-[resource-type]`

Examples: `stg-block-drop-site-bucket`, `prod-block-drop-github-deploy-role`, `shared-block-drop-terraform-state-bucket`.

Derive names in module locals from `var.environment`; do not scatter hard-coded legacy CDK names.

## State

- Remote state only: bucket `shared-block-drop-terraform-state-bucket` with S3 native locking (`use_lockfile = true`; Terraform >= 1.10).
- Keys: `bootstrap/`, `envs/stg/`, `envs/prod/`, `cloudflare/`, `grafana/` under that bucket.
- Do not reintroduce `dynamodb_table` in backends (deprecated).
- Never commit `*.tfstate` or `terraform.tfvars`.

## Regions

- Regional resources default to **`eu-north-1`** (see `block-drop-aws-regions` rule).
- ACM for CloudFront aliases stays in **`us-east-1`**.

## Environments

| Env | Domain |
|-----|--------|
| stg | `blockdrop-stg.7oas7er.com` |
| prod | `blockdrop.7oas7er.com` |

- GitHub OIDC provider is managed in **stg** only; prod looks it up via data source.
- **IAM**: define policies with `aws_iam_policy_document` data sources in `data.tf` (not inline `jsonencode` / heredoc JSON on the policy resource). Attach those documents from roles/policies elsewhere.
- **High-scores Lambda S3**: grant only `s3:GetObject` / `s3:PutObject` on `{bucket}/high-scores.json` (`local.high_scores_object_key`) — not bucket-wide `/*` or List/GetBucket wildcards.
- High-score buckets keep `prevent_destroy`; renaming forces replace — migrate objects first.
- Empty site buckets after replace cause CloudFront AccessDenied; sync `block-drop/` and invalidate.
- **Origin gate (Block Drop)**: CloudFront requires Cloudflare-injected `X-Origin-Verify`; keep AWS `origin_verify_secret` in sync with Cloudflare `stg_`/`prod_origin_verify_secret`. Apply Cloudflare before tightening CloudFront. See core rule *Cloudflare-only traffic* for the broader principle.
- **Cloudflare rate limit (Block Drop)**: zone `http_ratelimit` ruleset on `/api/scores` (IP + colo). Free plan allows one rule, path-only match, and 10s period/mitigation — do not add a second rule or `http.host` filters without upgrading.
- **www / apex → Block Drop**: keep ACM + CloudFront `aliases` on `blockdrop.7oas7er.com` only; Cloudflare Single Redirect 301s www/apex there (Free-compatible). Do not use Origin Rule Host-header override (Enterprise-only).
- **Access logs**: per-env `{env}-block-drop-access-logs-bucket` holds CloudFront standard logging v2 (`cloudfront/` via us-east-1 delivery APIs) and S3 site access logs (`s3-site/`). Prefer v2 over legacy `logging_config` (ACLs). Do not enable Parquet conversion unless needed.
- **Lambda logs / CW alarms**: manage `/aws/lambda/{env}-block-drop-high-scores-function` with finite retention (default 14d). Alarm on Lambda Errors/Throttles and CloudFront 5xxErrorRate (CF metrics in `us-east-1`). Prefer console/Grafana over adding a second paging SaaS; SNS is optional later.
